  <tr><td><strong>Nutritional Deviation (MAPE)</strong></td><td>18.4%</td><td><strong>6.2%</strong></td><td>-12.2%</td><td><strong>-66.3% (Lower Error)</strong></td></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>Intra-Plan Diversity Score</strong></td><td>48.0%</td><td><strong>94.0%</strong></td><td>+46.0%</td><td><strong>+95.8%</strong></td></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>Preference Satisfaction Rate</strong></td><td>42.5%</td><td><strong>88.0%</strong></td><td>+45.5%</td><td><strong>+107.1%</strong></td></tr>
</table>

<h2>4.2 Discussion and Analytical Insights</h2>
<p>The experimental results confirm that deterministic hard constraint filtering is essential to prevent allergen exposure (baseline suffered 25.8% failure). Furthermore, circadian slot partitioning and Jaccard diversity penalties reduced macro error to 6.2% and boosted diversity to 94.0%.</p>

