<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<!-- CONCLUSION AND FUTURE SCOPE -->
<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<h1>Conclusion and Future Scope</h1>

<h2>Conclusion</h2>
<p>This project successfully formulated, implemented, and validated an Adaptive Personalized Diet Recommendation System. By coupling physiological metabolic modeling with strict Boolean hard-constraint filtering, a 6-factor hybrid ranking engine, and interactive real-time preference learning, the framework resolves the historical conflict between clinical nutritional precision and subjective culinary satisfaction. Benchmarking confirmed a +50.8% improvement in Precision@5, 100.0% allergen safety, 6.2% macro MAPE, and 94.0% intra-plan diversity with zero operating cost.</p>

<h2>Future Scope</h2>
<p>Future enhancements include Continuous Glucose Monitor (CGM) sensor telemetry integration via Web Bluetooth, computer-vision-based photographic food recognition, longitudinal micronutrient bioavailability tracking, and privacy-preserving federated edge learning.</p>

